#!/usr/bin/env zsh
# FamilyOS blend configuration for live-sdk/libdevuansdk.
#
# Sourced by familyos.blend, which is itself sourced by live-sdk's `load`
# function AFTER live-sdk's own root config and libdevuansdk's core config
# have already run - see iso-builder/live-sdk/README.md for the full
# sourcing order. Every var/array assignment below either overrides an
# earlier default (plain `=`) or appends to one (`+=`).

# --- arch: CI-overridable, unlike every reference blend in the upstream
# repo (which hardcode `arch="amd64"` and expect a human to hand-edit this
# file before each build - see devuan-build-docs/confirmed-live-sdk.txt
# finding on the `load()`/config sourcing order). This lets one blend
# directory serve both amd64 and i386 via `ARCH=i386 zsh ...`, matching how
# live-build used two directories for the same purpose.
arch="${ARCH:-amd64}"

# blend_name: required by blend_postinst's own req array below (matching
# the reference blends' convention, unlike blend_preinst which doesn't
# need it).
blend_name="familyos"

# --- release: libdevuansdk's own core config defaults this to "beowulf"
# (Devuan 3, version "3.0.0" - confirmed directly against lib/libdevuansdk's
# vendored `config`, not assumed). Overridden here to daedalus (Devuan 5,
# bookworm-based) to match what the rest of this repo already targets and
# has verified package data for (devuan-build-docs/confirmed-*.txt).
release="daedalus"
version="5.0.0"

# image_name/vm_name: libdevuansdk's own root config computes these ONCE,
# textually, from ${os}/${release}/${version}/${arch}/${blend_name} at the
# point IT is sourced - which happens before this blend's config runs (see
# `load()`'s sourcing order in live-sdk's own `sdk` file: os_map's oslib is
# sourced, THEN blend_map's blendlib, which is what sources this file).
# Plain zsh variable assignment doesn't re-evaluate on later reads, so
# without this, image_name/vm_name would stay stamped with libdevuansdk's
# stale defaults ("devuan_beowulf_3.0.0_${arch}") regardless of the
# release="daedalus"/version="5.0.0"/blend_name="familyos" overrides above
# - silently wrong output filenames, and a same-run amd64+i386 matrix
# would collide on the same name. Recomputed here, AFTER release/version
# are overridden above (this recompute previously sat above the
# release/version overrides, which meant it still read their stale
# libdevuansdk defaults and produced exactly the wrong-codename filename
# this comment describes avoiding - confirmed via a real CI artifact named
# "devuan_beowulf_3.0.0_amd64_familyos-live.iso"; fixed by moving this
# block below the values it depends on).
image_name="${os}_${release}_${version}_${arch}_${blend_name}"
vm_name="${image_name}_virtual"

# --- mirror: deliberately deb.devuan.org, not libdevuansdk's own default
# of pkgmaster.devuan.org/merged - deb.devuan.org is the exact mirror this
# repo's devuan-build-docs/confirmed-*.txt files already SHA256-verified
# package data against, and what the live-build profiles already used.
mirror="http://deb.devuan.org/merged"

# libdevuansdk's own default `section="main contrib non-free"` is left
# unchanged (not narrowed to "main" the way the live-build profiles were) -
# that narrowing there was reacting to a live-build-specific concern
# (LB_MODE side effects landing in an already-passing CI stage, see
# devuan-build-docs/confirmed-live-build-package.txt). No equivalent
# concern exists here: libdevuansdk has no host-OS-driven mode switch, and
# firmware-linux-free (in base_packages, see below) is DFSG-free and lives
# in main anyway, so this default is being accepted as-is, not re-derived.

# --- Vendor-default package name corrections. Both live-sdk's own root
# `config` and libdevuansdk's own root `config` (sourced before this file,
# see the sourcing-order comment at the top) carry obsolete package names
# in their unconditional base/extra_packages arrays - the exact same class
# of bug as live-build's own casper/linux-amd64 internal defaults, just in
# a different tool. Confirmed against a real CI build failure
# ("Package btrfs-tools is not available, but is referred to by another
# package") and a fresh check against Devuan's real daedalus package
# indexes (see devuan-build-docs/confirmed-package-sweep.txt for the full
# sweep, not just these three). Fixed here, blend-side, via zsh's
# `${array:#pattern}` element-removal syntax - NOT by patching either
# vendored config file directly, which would silently be reverted the next
# time either pinned commit SHA is bumped.
#
# - btrfs-tools: renamed to btrfs-progs in Debian years before daedalus:
#   libdevuansdk's own base_packages still has the old name, and it simply
#   doesn't exist in daedalus's index - this is the package that actually
#   broke the CI build. FamilyOS has no btrfs requirement anywhere (the
#   live filesystem is squashfs+overlayfs, persistence is a plain
#   ext4/FAT partition per iso-builder/live-build/persistence-media/) -
#   excluded outright rather than renamed to btrfs-progs, since there's no
#   real use for it on this project's target hardware.
base_packages=(${base_packages:#btrfs-tools})
#
# - git-core: the old (pre-2009) Debian package name for git, long since
#   merged into a single "git" package - libdevuansdk's own base_packages
#   still has the old name, and it doesn't exist in daedalus's index
#   either. Swapped for the current name rather than excluded, since
#   nothing suggests libdevuansdk intended to NOT have git available.
base_packages=(${base_packages:#git-core})
base_packages+=(git)
#
# - firmware-linux: live-sdk's own top-level `config` (sourced
#   unconditionally by the `sdk` file for every build, not something this
#   blend controls) lists this in extra_packages. It does not exist in
#   daedalus's main, contrib, OR non-free component (checked all three
#   directly against the real index - this isn't a matter of enabling a
#   broader archive area). Debian 12/bookworm reorganized non-free
#   firmware packaging around a new non-free-firmware archive component
#   this project doesn't enable (predates daedalus; libdevuansdk hasn't
#   been touched since 2021) - "firmware-linux" as a single umbrella
#   metapackage doesn't survive that reorganization. Excluded outright:
#   libdevuansdk's own base_packages already includes firmware-linux-free
#   (DFSG-free, confirmed present in main) separately, so this isn't a net
#   loss of firmware coverage, just removal of a broken duplicate.
extra_packages=(${extra_packages:#firmware-linux})
#
# - cryptsetup: live-sdk's own top-level `config` lists this unconditionally
#   in the same extra_packages block as firmware-linux above (real, exists
#   fine in daedalus's index - this one isn't a naming/availability bug).
#   Installing it triggers a real, confirmed build.log warning ("insserv:
#   FATAL: service cryptdisks-early has to be enabled to use service
#   cryptdisks" right after "Setting up cryptsetup") - non-fatal to the
#   build, but FamilyOS is a toddler-facing live/kiosk system with no
#   disk-encryption requirement anywhere in this repo's docs. Excluded
#   outright here, same as firmware-linux above, rather than installing it
#   just to purge it again in familyos.blend's finalize script (which
#   would repeat the exact install-then-immediately-undo churn the
#   purge_packages/dbus fix above exists to avoid) or fixing the
#   cryptdisks-early enable-ordering to keep a feature nothing here uses.
extra_packages=(${extra_packages:#cryptsetup})

# --- kernel package: real, verified package names from
# devuan-build-docs/confirmed-kernel-packages.txt, NOT copied from
# live-sdk's own bundled example config (its root `config` uses
# "linux-image-686" for i386, which is the non-PAE flavour Debian/Devuan
# dropped after stretch - see iso-builder/live-build/i386/auto/config's
# own comment on the same point). 686-pae is required for the target
# hardware (single-core Atom netbooks needing PAE) per
# Project_Vault/_Base Architecture Overview.md.
#
# For i386, live-sdk's own root `config` has already unconditionally added
# "linux-image-686" to extra_packages by the time this file runs (its own
# `case "$arch" in i386) extra_packages+=(linux-image-686) ;; ... esac`,
# sourced before any blend loads) - not a nonexistent-package bug like
# btrfs-tools/git-core/firmware-linux above (linux-image-686 is real), but
# installing both kernel flavours side by side on the same i386 build
# defeats the entire point of choosing 686-pae. Stripped here for the same
# "fix in the blend, not the vendored file" reason as those three. Doesn't
# change anything for the amd64-only build this CI currently runs (amd64's
# vendor default and this blend's own choice are already the same
# package), but matters the moment an i386 build is ever run.
extra_packages=(${extra_packages:#linux-image-686})
case "$arch" in
	amd64) extra_packages+=(linux-image-amd64) ;;
	i386)  extra_packages+=(linux-image-686-pae) ;;
esac

# --- FamilyOS package set: carried over verbatim from
# iso-builder/live-build/common/package-lists/familyos.list.chroot. Not
# re-derived from scratch - the requirement (which packages FamilyOS
# needs) didn't change with the build tool, only how they get installed.
# live-boot is NOT listed here: libdevuansdk's core iso_prepare_strap
# installs `live-boot live-boot-initramfs-tools` unconditionally, before
# any blend code runs - listing it again would be harmless but redundant
# (see devuan-build-docs/confirmed-live-sdk.txt).
extra_packages+=(
	openbox
	xinit
	xserver-xorg
	alsa-utils
	sudo
	whiptail
	pamtester
	python3-pyqt5
	python3-pyqt5.qtwebengine
	gcompris-qt
	tuxpaint
	tuxmath
	tuxtype
	mpv
	iptables
	isc-dhcp-client
	papirus-icon-theme
	live-config-sysvinit
	# sysvinit-core, explicitly: libdevuansdk's own core_packages (its root
	# config) lists plain "sysvinit", not "sysvinit-core" - the former is
	# not guaranteed to actually be the package that installs as PID 1 on
	# a modern Devuan release the way sysvinit-core is (this repo's old
	# familyos.list.chroot listed sysvinit-core explicitly for exactly
	# this reason). Redundant-but-safe if libdevuansdk's own default turns
	# out fine; not redundant if it doesn't.
	sysvinit-core
)

# NOT here: a "live-config-systemd-" apt removal-suffix entry, matching
# the old familyos.list.chroot's de-select guard (Debian bug #772651).
# bootstrap_stage4 (libdevuansdk/zlibs/bootstrap) pre-flights every
# extra_packages entry with an exact-match `apt-cache search` existence
# check before installing anything, with no special-casing for apt's own
# trailing "-" removal syntax - "live-config-systemd-" would be reported
# as a nonexistent package and hard-fail the entire build. The same
# protective intent is instead applied as an explicit `apt-get purge` in
# familyos.blend's finalize script, which runs after stage4 and isn't
# subject to that preflight check.

# Plymouth is deliberately NOT in extra_packages, for the exact reason
# given in the live-build hook this replaces
# (iso-builder/live-build/common/hooks/live/0040-optional-plymouth.hook.chroot):
# stage4's package install (bootstrap_stage4 in libdevuansdk/zlibs/bootstrap)
# fails its ENTIRE apt-get invocation - and therefore the whole build - if
# any one package in extra_packages is unsatisfiable, and Plymouth's
# systemd-vs-elogind dependency situation on Devuan daedalus is unverified.
# It's attempted separately, with explicit failure tolerance, in
# familyos.blend's blend_postinst below.

# --- purge_packages: libdevuansdk's own core config unconditionally
# purges `dbus` at the end of bootstrap_stage3 (base_packages install),
# which cascade-removes every package base_packages pulled in only as an
# automatic dependency of dbus - confirmed via a real build.log: the GTK/
# desktop stack (adwaita-icon-theme, libcairo2, libgtk-3-0, etc., ~171MB)
# gets installed, purged, then reinstalled from scratch a few minutes
# later in bootstrap_stage4 once FamilyOS's own extra_packages (openbox,
# xserver-xorg, python3-pyqt5, ...) need that same dbus/GTK stack again.
# Pure download+install+purge+reinstall churn, not a correctness issue -
# harmless for a blend that never needs dbus, but this one does. Excluded
# here rather than patched in the vendored file, same reasoning and same
# `${array:#pattern}` idiom as the base_packages/extra_packages
# corrections above.
purge_packages=(${purge_packages:#dbus})
